@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Browser layer — Playwright and agent-browser share one Chromium, and every harness is told

' covers: defs/base-node-browser/**
' covers: defs/base-node-browser/skills/agent-browser/SKILL.md
' covers: defs/base-node-browser/build.sh
' covers: defs/base-node-browser/ensure.sh
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: defs/cursor/tests/test_tools.sh
' covers: defs/opencode/tests/test_tools.sh
' covers: defs/claudecode/tests/test_tools.sh
'
' ── ONE CHROMIUM, ENFORCED BY A GUARD RATHER THAN BY A COMMENT ──────────────
' PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION=1.61.0, PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/opt/ms-playwright.
'
' `playwright install chromium` lands TWO browsers — `chromium-<rev>` and
' `chromium_headless_shell-<rev>` — and this layer only ever launches the first.
' The symlink below proves it: its `find … -path '*/chromium-*/*'` uses a HYPHEN
' so it cannot match the shell. Measured at 1.61.0: chromium 624 MB, headless
' shell **334 MB**, ffmpeg 3.3 MB — i.e. a quarter of the layer was installed and
' then excluded by hand. `--no-shell` stops installing it at all.
'
' The trade, stated so nobody rediscovers it: Playwright >=1.49 PREFERS the shell
' for its own headless runs, so a project's `playwright test` falls back to full
' Chromium — slower to start, same result — while agent-browser, which drives
' Chromium over CDP, never wanted the shell at all.
'
' The `! ls -d "$PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH"/chromium_headless_shell-*` line in the
' same RUN is the point of the flag: a future Playwright that ignores
' `--no-shell` must fail this build LOUDLY rather than quietly re-adding 334 MB
' to three variants. Pinned by internal/contract
' TestBrowserLayerInstallsOneChromiumNotTwo.
'
' ── WHAT THE BUILD CAN AND CANNOT VERIFY ────────────────────────────────────
' The install RUN asserts everything reachable from a buildkit step:
' `agent-browser --version`, `test -x "$AGENT_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH"`,
' `test -f "$AGENT_BROWSER_SKILLS_DIR/core/SKILL.md"`. Verified 2026-09-01 on the
' darwin build of 0.36.0: with the executable path set it launches headless and
' never asks for `install`.
'
' The Linux run-as-uid path (containers auto-enable --no-sandbox since 0.16.1) is
' deliberately NOT asserted here — a buildkit RUN is not the container the image
' will run in. It is covered by defs/base-node-browser/ensure.sh's floor probe
' and by each def's tests/test_tools.sh.
'
' The floor probe is the layer's contract restated as a runnable check: node,
' playwright and typescript-language-server on PATH, a `chromium-*` directory
' under the browser store, `agent-browser` on PATH, an executable
' AGENT_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH, core/SKILL.md under AGENT_BROWSER_SKILLS_DIR,
' and /opt/proveo/skills/agent-browser/SKILL.md present for the seed to copy.
'
' Both the browser store and /opt/agent-browser are `chmod -R a+rX`: the harness
' never runs as root, so an arbitrary run-as uid must be able to launch Chromium,
' and a repo-local Playwright honours the same PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH — so a
' project's own `npx playwright install` lands in the same shared store.
'
' agent-browser is pinned by version AND tarball digest:
'   ARG AGENT_BROWSER_VERSION=0.36.0
'   ARG AGENT_BROWSER_SHA256=858a753760034d73c6bc17dd895f91141ef03c3fcca978348b378e26d2d617e4
' The tarball ships every platform's binary (~40 MB); only this arch's is kept.
'
' ── WHY A DISCOVERY STUB RATHER THAN A COPIED GUIDE ────────────────────────
' The layer pins agent-browser the way it pins Playwright: by VERSION and by
' DIGEST of the tarball it unpacks, and it points the binary at the Chromium
' Playwright already installed rather than letting `agent-browser install` fetch
' a second one. A layer that drifts on any of these rebuilds into something the
' floor probe and the seed no longer describe.
'
' Knob: PROVEO_BROWSER_SKILL=off.
'
' The stub is proveo's own file, so it is REFRESHED IN PLACE while an operator's
' own skills beside it are never touched. The comparison uses `sha256sum` piped
' from both files rather than `cmp`, because diffutils is not on the slim floor —
' and copying unconditionally would rewrite an unchanged file on every start.
'
' The `-browser` image variants (FROM proveo/base-node-browser) carry
' Playwright's Chromium and vercel-labs/agent-browser pointed at it. The binary
' alone is not discoverable by an agent, so the seed drops agent-browser's
' discovery STUB into the harness's USER-level skills directory — the one place
' every harness reads without a project edit. The stub only tells the agent to
' run `agent-browser skills get core`, which serves the guide matching the
' INSTALLED version, so nothing here goes stale when the binary moves.
'
'   claudecode  ~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
'   cursor      ~/.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md  (also reads ~/.agents/skills)
'   opencode    ~/.config/opencode/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
'               (also reads ~/.claude/skills)
'   cecli       NONE — no browser variant and no skills directory. A decision,
'               so the case is spelled out rather than falling through.
'
' Gated on the BINARY, not the image name: a non-browser image has no
' agent-browser and gets no skill, so the agent is never handed a tool it lacks.

cloud "registry.npmjs.org\n""agent-browser-<v>.tgz""" as NPM <<cloud>>

node "Image build — defs/base-node-browser/Dockerfile" as BUILD <<host>> {
  component "Playwright ""<v>""\n""playwright install --with-deps --no-shell chromium""" as PW <<app>>
  database "browser store\n""/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-<rev>/chrome-linux/chrome""" as STORE <<db>>
  component "agent-browser (native Rust)\n""/usr/local/bin/agent-browser""" as AB <<app>>
  database "skill-data\n""AGENT_BROWSER_SKILLS_DIR=/opt/agent-browser/skill-data""" as SKD <<db>>
  component "revision-stable symlink\n""AGENT_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH=/opt/proveo/chromium/chrome""" as LINK <<app>>
  component "discovery stub\n""/opt/proveo/skills/agent-browser/SKILL.md""" as STUB <<db>>
}

node "Seed — ""proveo_seed <target>"" (both backends)" as SEED <<host>> {
  component "proveo_seed_browser_skills\ngated on ""command -v agent-browser""" as SEEDFN <<app>>
}

node "Agent home (user level)" as HOME <<host>> {
  component "claudecode ""~/.claude/skills/""" as H1 <<app>>
  component "cursor ""~/.cursor/skills/""" as H2 <<app>>
  component "opencode ""~/.config/opencode/skills/""" as H3 <<app>>
}

component "agent, any harness\n""agent-browser skills get core"" → ""open"" · ""snapshot"" · ""click""" as AGENT <<app>>
component "headless Chromium (CDP)" as CHROME <<app>>

component "a SECOND Chromium\n""agent-browser install"" · Chrome for Testing" as DUP <<error>>
component "'Skills directory not found'\nbinary without the npm skill tree" as NOSK <<error>>

NPM   ARROW_CLOUD AB : pinned version + sha256,\none arch's binary kept
NPM   ARROW_CLOUD SKD : the same tarball
PW    ARROW_MAIN STORE
STORE ARROW_MAIN LINK : ""find chromium-*/…/chrome"" at build
LINK  ARROW_MAIN AB : the browser it launches
SKD   ARROW_MAIN AB
STUB  ARROW_MAIN SEEDFN
SEEDFN ARROW_MAIN H1
SEEDFN ARROW_MAIN H2
SEEDFN ARROW_MAIN H3
H1    ARROW_MAIN AGENT
H2    ARROW_MAIN AGENT
H3    ARROW_MAIN AGENT
AGENT ARROW_MAIN AB
AB    ARROW_MAIN CHROME : ""--no-sandbox"" auto in containers,\nany run-as uid, HOME writable
AB    ARROW_ERROR DUP : never — the executable\npath is already set
AB    ARROW_ERROR NOSK : never — the tree ships\nbeside the binary

note right of BUILD
  **Two clients, one browser.** Playwright is
  the project's test runner and library;
  agent-browser is the agent's interactive
  tool. Both launch the Chromium Playwright
  installed, so the layer pays for it once.
end note

note left of PW
  **--no-shell, and a guard that proves it.**
  ""playwright install"" lands chromium AND
  chromium_headless_shell; only the first is
  ever launched. Measured at 1.61.0: 624 MB
  against **334 MB** installed then excluded.
end note

note bottom of PW
  **The ""! ls"" line is the point of the flag.**
  A future Playwright that ignores ""--no-shell""
  must fail this build loudly rather than
  quietly re-adding 334 MB to three variants.
end note

note bottom of AB
  **A buildkit RUN is not the container it will
  run in.** So the layer verifies what it can —
  ""--version"", the executable path, the skills
  file — and the run-as-uid launch is left to
  ensure.sh's floor probe and defs/*/tests.
end note

note bottom of STORE
  **World-readable because root never runs.**
  An arbitrary run-as uid has to launch
  Chromium, so the store and the skill tree are
  ""chmod -R a+rX"" — and a repo-local Playwright
  honours the same variable and lands here too.
end note

note bottom of NPM
  **The tarball, not ""npm install -g"".** The
  package wants Node ≥ 24 on a Node 22 floor;
  its JS launcher only execs the native
  binary. Pinning the digest makes the layer
  reproducible and the floor probe honest.
end note

note bottom of SEED
  **Discoverability is the seed's job.** A
  binary on PATH is invisible to an agent;
  the stub in the user skills dir is what it
  reads. It says only ""skills get core"", so
  the guide always matches the binary.
end note

note right of HOME
  **User level, never the workspace.** The
  checkout is the operator's; a skill seeded
  there would mutate it. Every harness reads
  a home directory, and the table names
  cecli's (empty) case on purpose.
end note

@enduml
